	"generatedBy": "hand-drawn, pre-registered before any GLM inference ran",
	"drawnFrom": "research/v3/data/oracle-premise/eval-set.json, the 142 included entries",
	"selectionRule": "Ranked over the 142 by the number of DISTINCT human review rounds that touched the cover, then by total human label count. The point of the probe is a GLM x Qwen x REVIEWER triangle, and a triangle needs its third vertex, so the draw maximizes reviewer-label overlap rather than sampling at random.",
	"whatTheReviewerLabelsAre": "Overwhelmingly SAM `mask_correct.<noun>` verdicts from the sam-mask-quality-{1,2,3,3b} rounds plus residual-purity-{1,2} — a human saying that a NAMED NOUN is present on the cover and correctly delimited. That is noun ground truth, and the noun question (variant J) is the probe's live consumer. Direct reviewer answers to has_dominant_subject / subject_kind exist for only three of the 142 (ranks 9, 21, 22 below); the bcde-validation-1 round was drawn from the coverage-set core, which barely intersects eval-142.",
	"caveat": "THIS IS NOT A RANDOM 30. It is conditioned on prior review attention, and prior review attention was itself partly conditioned on MODEL DISAGREEMENT — residual-purity strata are `noun-fired`/`noun-silent`, and bcde-gate-reconciliation-1 is an explicitly contradiction-conditioned population. PREMISE_NEXT.md §3 and §15.9 both require that a round conditioned on disagreement be reported as a different population. Any agreement rate measured here is therefore an estimate on a review-enriched slice of eval-142, not on eval-142 and not on the corpus.",
	"joinKey": "artwork_id — NOT sha256. The SAM and residual rounds record the composited review-overlay PNG's sha256, not the cover's, so a sha256 join silently drops ~70% of the usable reviewer signal. sha256 is carried below only as a same-bytes qualifier and as the resolution key into eval-set.json.",
	"eIsFAgreement": "23 of the 30 have E==F agreement on BOTH has_dominant_subject and subject_kind (the Qwen arm's own two-wording corroboration). The 7 that disagree are kept deliberately: a cover where Qwen's two wordings disagree is exactly where an out-of-family second opinion would earn its keep.",
